{"title":"","link":"http://scripting.com/2025/04/22.html#a004359","date":1745369039000,"content":"<img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/scripting.com/images/2020/03/12/usAttacked.png\" />It's crazy to even think of moving Chrome from Google <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/22/openai-exec-says-the-company-would-buy-googles-chrome-browser-if-offered-the-chance/?guccounter=1&amp;guce_referrer=aHR0cDovL3NjcmlwdGluZy5jb20v&amp;guce_referrer_sig=AQAAALnjUkq94tpAXWEMr56Y1XtRJG6hrCFHhLQc0kOdOGX9lwkrh2G9cxd1P5OT3HH7-uCaybLWdPHi3J-VkpdtBV16Lnb8xCbvEIsQgOME7IXZgson6x4kIgRZgxaHkn8aH76hT-4BjuIa-Xbn30WQDKJ1N-mHp3PfPONGELKM0nVn\">to OpenAI</a>. The web needs to not be owned by anyone, esp not owned by the tech industry. What Google tried to do to the web is obscene. I love ChatGPT, but let's keep Chrome out of their owner's greedy little hands. Set it up so it stands alone.","author":"","siteTitle":"Scripting News","siteHash":"d6ad59631287cc248e52fdfe0c4f962c0fd08643d455b40f799700d8b2f97c65","entryHash":"3cab1a7f71e3c67bb01a64c2db0d9845e30cebde56fd76368690f224991eeedb","category":"Sites"}